          %h2#References References
          %p Freyd first introduced essentially algebraic theories here:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Aspects of Topoi
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/B65FB15DCD85C816F31D9C87D355AD24/S0004972700044828a.pdf/aspects-of-topoi.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Ad%C3%A1mek"}> Jiří Adámek
                , M. Hébert,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On essentially algebraic theories and their generalizations
            %li#AdamekRosicky
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Ad%C3%A1mek"}> Jiří Adámek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locally+presentable+and+accessible+categories"} Locally presentable and accessible categories
          %p A nice equivalent formulation can be found in
          %ul
            %li#PalmgrenVickers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Palmgren"}> Erik Palmgren
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Vickers"} Steve Vickers
              Partial Horn logic and cartesian categories. Annals of Pure and Applied Logic, 145(2007), 314-355. (
              %a{:href => "http://www2.math.uu.se/~palmgren/partialalgebras_pre.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Cartesian theories were introduced under different names in the early seventies by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Isbell"} John Isbell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"} Peter Freyd
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Coste"} Michel Coste
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone79"} Johnstone 1979
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone02"} 2002
          %ul
            %li#Freyd02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
                ,
                %em Cartesian Logic
                , Theor. Comp. Sci.
                %strong 278
                (2002) pp.3-21.
            %li#Johnstone79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em A Syntactic Approach to Diers’ Localizable Categories
                , pp.466-478 in Springer LNM
                %strong 753
                Heidelberg 1979.
            %li#Johnstone02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em
                  Sketches of an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
                  II
                , Oxford UP 2002. (Around D1.3.4 p.833)
          %p A short introductory/overview note:
          %ul
            %li#keml-diagrams
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Nuyts"}> Andreas Nuyts
              ,
